==German==

===Etymology===
From a conflation of {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|anelich}}, {{m|gmh|enlich||alike; similar}} (from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|anagilih}}, from {{m|goh|ana}} + {{m|goh|gilih}}) and {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|einlich}}, {{m|gmh|enlich||uniform; consistent}}. Cognate with {{cog|dum|aenlijck}}, {{cog|enm|anlike}}, {{m|enm|anlyke}}, {{m|enm|anlich}}, {{m|enm|onlich}}, {{cog|non|álíkr}}. More at {{l|en|alike}}; {{l|en|only}}.

